{{- /*
Builds the Build Output API configuration for the Vercel projects.
scripts/build-vercel.sh moves it to .vercel/output/config.json. vercel.json
cannot carry these routes: Vercel reads it before the build runs.

The first route adds "X-Robots-Tag: noindex" to every response, unless the
build sets HUGO_PARAMS_INDEXABLE. Only the chainguard-docs production project
does. The header can't live in vercel.json, because every project that builds
this repository reads the same vercel.json, and a preview must never be
indexed: its canonical links point at itself, so it would compete with the
real docs in search results.

The other routes reproduce production nginx, in the order nginx applies them:

1. Every redirect rule from layouts/partials/redirect-rules.html, as a 301. A
   route matches the path without the query string, and Vercel carries the
   query over to the Location, which is what nginx does.

2. The trailing-slash redirect, which keeps the site's base path. nginx adds the slash only when the path is a
   directory, which a route cannot test, so here a missing path is redirected
   too and then answers 404. Every real directory behaves as in production.
   This runs before the filesystem, because Vercel otherwise serves a
   directory's index.html without the slash.

3. The filesystem, then /page.md (or /page.md/) served from /page/index.md,
   then the 404 page.

Routes stop at the first match, except the noindex route, which continues to
the next one. The other response headers come from vercel.json, which Vercel
applies to every response, redirects included.

A preview build (HUGO_PARAMS_EMULATEWWW, set by scripts/build-vercel.sh) is
served the way production is served behind www.chainguard.dev. In production,
www removes a trailing slash with a 308, then rewrites /docs/<path> to /<path>
on the chainguard-docs project, which serves its files from its root. A
preview has nothing in front of it, so build-vercel.sh puts its files under
/docs/ instead, and this template:

- puts /docs in front of every route pattern below, so each route matches
  the path a reader requests;
- adds two routes ahead of them: / goes to the docs home, because Vercel's PR
  comments link to the preview's root, and a trailing slash is removed with a
  308, as www does.

A path outside /docs has no file, so it answers 404, as www does for the docs.
A page that loads a file from the host root, such as /fonts/x.woff2, fails on
the preview as it would in production.
*/ -}}
{{- $basePath := strings.TrimSuffix "/" site.Home.RelPermalink -}}
{{- /* Where the files are served: under the base path on a preview, at the
       host root in production. */ -}}
{{- $servedPath := "" -}}
{{- if site.Params.emulatewww -}}
{{- $servedPath = $basePath -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $routes := slice -}}
{{- if not site.Params.indexable -}}
{{- $routes = $routes | append (dict
  "src" `^/.*$`
  "headers" (dict "X-Robots-Tag" "noindex")
  "continue" true) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- if $servedPath -}}
{{- $routes = $routes | append
  (dict "src" `^/$` "status" 308 "headers" (dict "Location" $servedPath))
  (dict "src" (printf `^(%s(/.*)?)/$` $servedPath) "status" 308 "headers" (dict "Location" "$1")) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- range partial "redirect-rules.html" . -}}
{{- if and $servedPath (not (strings.HasPrefix .regex "^/")) -}}
{{- errorf "index.vercelconfig.json: redirect rule %q doesn't start with ^/, so it can't be served under %s" .regex $servedPath -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $routes = $routes | append (dict
  "src" (printf "^%s%s" $servedPath (strings.TrimPrefix "^" .regex))
  "caseSensitive" .caseSensitive
  "status" 301
  "headers" (dict "Location" .target)) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{- $routes = $routes | append
  (dict "src" (printf `^%s([^.]*[^/])$` $servedPath) "status" 301 "headers" (dict "Location" (printf "%s$1/" $basePath)))
  (dict "handle" "filesystem")
  (dict "src" `^(.+)\.md/?$` "dest" "$1/index.md" "check" true)
  (dict "handle" "error")
  (dict "src" `^/.*$` "status" 404 "dest" "/404.html") -}}
{{- dict "version" 3 "routes" $routes | jsonify (dict "indent" "  ") -}}
